<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danishmendids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1075–<a href="/years/1178">1178</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Danishmendid dynasty, Danishmendid emirate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danishmendids were a Turkmen dynasty that ruled north-central and north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, from cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokat">Tokat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niksar">Niksar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatya">Malatya</a>, from the late eleventh century. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmend-gazi">Danishmend Gazi</a>, they captured Bohemond of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> in 1100 and were at first stronger than the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum. They were weakened by internal divisions and annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-ii">Kilij Arslan II</a> by 1178.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danishmendids.jpg" alt="Danishmendids" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapMaster · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatolia_1097.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
